# Change requests

When the owner wants UI/feature/page/journey changes on the existing site, use the change-request pipeline — not a one-shot “just build it” unless they explicitly waive gates.

1. Prefer `/product-change` (or create `docs/change-requests/CR-*.md` from `_TEMPLATE.md`).
2. Stages in order: **BA → Designer → Developer → QA**.
3. **Owner gate** after each stage (`approved` in the CR table) before the next role.
4. Do not run Cloud Agents, Automations, or parallel writers on the same files unless the owner asks.
5. Subagents `ba-analyst`, `designer`, `developer`, `qa-reviewer` match those stages; `content-guard` is optional before ship.
6. Keep MVP informational; mark unknowns `NEEDS OWNER INPUT`.
7. Design source of truth: `docs/design-guidelines.md` + the Next.js site (no Figma redraw unless asked).
